        "y0": 0.4719061409775831,
        "x1": 0.879530142134979,
        "y1": 0.4861047160313985
      },
      "text": "for finite correspondences whose numerical dynamical degrees are a log-concave sequence. In",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.12100871110162816,
        "y0": 0.49171625350263515,
        "x1": 0.5421180019859506,
        "y1": 0.5059148285564504
      },
      "text": "the general case, the numerical dynamical degrees λ",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.542117694245667,
        "y0": 0.49858689251535016,
        "x1": 0.5495798832228204,
        "y1": 0.5080525812796912
      },
      "text": "k",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5505879891018908,
        "y0": 0.49171625350263515,
        "x1": 0.8795299369747899,
        "y1": 0.5059148285564504
      },
      "text": "(f) may not be log-concave. The second",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.12100865981158088,
        "y0": 0.511668733066731,
        "x1": 0.8795305524553572,
        "y1": 0.5258673081205463
      },
      "text": "main idea in [Xie24] is (see Theorem 1.14 therein, and Proposition 1.4 below) to establish some",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.12100840336134454,
        "y0": 0.5314784831502375,
        "x1": 0.8831604516806723,
        "y1": 0.5456770582040529
      },
      "text": "interesting relations between certain polytopes of two sequences satisfying certain properties.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.12040164210215336,
        "y0": 0.5514309627143335,
        "x1": 0.8793280593487395,
        "y1": 0.5656295377681487
      },
      "text": "Theorem 1.14 in [Xie24] can be viewed as a continuous version of Lemma 4.9 in [HT24] (see",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.12100840336134454,
        "y0": 0.5712404953329127,
        "x1": 0.30937833385307245,
        "y1": 0.585439070386728
      },
      "text": "Proposition 1.4 below).",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.14117630389558167,
        "y0": 0.5939013193452161,
        "x1": 0.7165731349913012,
        "y1": 0.6080998943990313
      },
      "text": "To prove Theorem 1.1, here we replace the cohomological operator G",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7165721733029149,
        "y0": 0.6007718133813129,
        "x1": 0.7230259486607142,
        "y1": 0.610237502145654
      },
      "text": "r",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.730689810103729,
        "y0": 0.5939011743685978,
        "x1": 0.8795305524553572,
        "y1": 0.6080997494224132
      },
      "text": "in the approach in",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1210091214220063,
        "y0": 0.6138536539326938,
        "x1": 0.4624537876674107,
        "y1": 0.628052228986509
      },
      "text": "[HT24] by composing with iterations of F",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.46527699702928044,
        "y0": 0.6134560351700228,
        "x1": 0.47233584107471116,
        "y1": 0.6229217239343638
      },
      "text": "∗",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.4731426848082983,
        "y0": 0.6138536901768483,
        "x1": 0.8793293928899685,
        "y1": 0.6280522652306636
      },
      "text": ". There is a complication arising in case f is not a",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.12100799304096639,
        "y0": 0.6336638027019003,
        "x1": 0.879733661042542,
        "y1": 0.6478623777557155
      },
      "text": "finite correspondence: in this case the dynamical degree is not the spectral radius but involves",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.12100799304096639,
        "y0": 0.6536162822659961,
        "x1": 0.5348567161239496,
        "y1": 0.6678148573198115
      },
      "text": "norms of dynamical iterates of the correspondence f",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.537074651637999,
        "y0": 0.6532186272591707,
        "x1": 0.5509907698430935,
        "y1": 0.6626843160235117
      },
      "text": "♦t",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.551998516691833,
        "y0": 0.6536162822659961,
        "x1": 0.8151917529707196,
        "y1": 0.6678148573198115
      },
      "text": ". In case the dynamical degrees λ",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8151914965204832,
        "y0": 0.6604869212787112,
        "x1": 0.8226536854976365,
        "y1": 0.6699526100430522
      },
      "text": "k",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8236624581473214,
        "y0": 0.6536162822659961,
        "x1": 0.8793271361278887,
        "y1": 0.6678148573198115
      },
      "text": "(f) are",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.12100768530068277,
        "y0": 0.6734263947910482,
        "x1": 0.8829579585740546,
        "y1": 0.6876249698448634
      },
      "text": "a log-concave sequence, then again Lemma 4.9 in [HT24] can be used to conclude Theorem 1.1.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.12100840336134454,
        "y0": 0.6933786387681395,
        "x1": 0.8795286034335609,
        "y1": 0.7075772138219548
      },
      "text": "In the general case, we make use of special properties of the Frobenius norm on matrices and",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.12100840336134454,
        "y0": 0.713188261997105,
        "x1": 0.8793277516084559,
        "y1": 0.7273868370509204
      },
      "text": "of asymptotic singular values of powers of a matrix (this property was used in [Hu19, Hu24]",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.12100840336134454,
        "y0": 0.7331411040027465,
        "x1": 0.8795306550354517,
        "y1": 0.7473396790565617
      },
      "text": "to solve Dynamical degree comparison conjecture for endomorphisms of Abelian varieties), as",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.12020166220785189,
        "y0": 0.7529511984057211,
        "x1": 0.8799338973870798,
        "y1": 0.7671497734595365
      },
      "text": "well as use essentially the second main idea in [Xie24] mentioned above, but in the following",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.12100840336134454,
        "y0": 0.7729035692373534,
        "x1": 0.8795300395548844,
        "y1": 0.7871021442911688
      },
      "text": "form which is similar to the form of Lemma 4.9 in [HT24]. (More precisely, in Lemma 4.9 in",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.12100840336134454,
        "y0": 0.792713663640328,
        "x1": 0.8795314756762079,
        "y1": 0.8069122386941434
      },
      "text": "[HT24], Condition 2 below is required, but instead of Condition 1 below it is required that the",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.12101004464285714,
        "y0": 0.8126660344719604,
        "x1": 0.20995124368106619,
        "y1": 0.8268646095257757
      },
      "text": "sequence a",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20995108981092436,
        "y0": 0.8195366916067527,
        "x1": 0.2157998477711397,
        "y1": 0.8290023803710938
      },
      "text": "j",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.22245568027015494,
        "y0": 0.8126660344719604,
        "x1": 0.3501197109703256,
        "y1": 0.8268646095257757
      },
      "text": "is log-concave.)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.12100996770778624,
        "y0": 0.8405994043780619,
        "x1": 0.25613639254529935,
        "y1": 0.8547979794318772
      },
      "text": "Proposition 1.4.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
